From d4f2184b9cbcf69acf576a241a79d2e65d51e31b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AF9 <af9@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:56:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fusion reactors: magnetic field instead of standby power;
 Mk1-Mk3 rings 19/23/27 blocks, ring render scales (7.5.3-af9.14)

- FusionReactorMachine: the 4 A standby / 1 A running power is gone. The reactor builds a magnetic field (Mk1 1,000, Mk2 4,000,
  Mk3 16,000, above 64,000; 1 % of it per tick for 1 A of its voltage) from the auxiliary hatches, else the primary ones. A
  reaction starts at its min_field (recipe data, else eu_to_start / 160,000) and a run drains decay_rate (else a quarter of
  min_field); below the minimum it waits. The field collapses with the structure. Adapted from CosmicCore's
  MagneticFieldMachine (LGPL-3.0).
- FusionStructure: the ring's centre row and column are repeated, so the ring is 19 / 23 / 27 blocks wide with the same shape.
  The ring render follows.
- New tooltip with field, size and run rules; controller screen and recipe label show the field.
